{
  "dom_id": "step-q165768",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $t(x)={x}^{4}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{4}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{4})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}\\cdot (\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3})^{′} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}{sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{3} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}+3{x}^{6}{sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}(4\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}+3{x}^{3}{sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
